# A call into a family runs one of its overrides: `Handler.handle` and `Handler.log` each run their own body or
# `ClickHandler`'s, on the Handler the caller calls them on. What the caller hands the base's method is what the override
# is handed: `handle` an Event, `log` a Click, each a value from beyond. The base's own body (the dispatch's own arrow)
# reads the value it is handed, not the Handler. Each result, a string, goes back to the dispatch that ran it.
# the override's result has the dispatch's own moment: closed, its line into the dispatch is dropped, open it is drawn
known #102 fault more t:clean.shapes.Circle@n:clean.shapes.Factory/clean.shapes.Factory.make>n:clean.shapes.Factory/clean.shapes.Factory.make
known #102 fault no line Circle@Factory()/Factory.make > Factory()/Factory.make

route clean.handlers.Handler
step Handler()/Handler.handle
step Handler()/Handler.handle/ClickHandler.handle
step Handler()/Handler.log
step Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log

line entry > Handler()/Handler.handle call
line entry > Handler()/Handler.log call
known #100 line Handler > Handler()/Handler.handle/ClickHandler.handle value
known #100 line Handler > Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log value
known #126 line Event > Handler()/Handler.handle value                  # handle's own body reads e.name
line Event > Handler()/Handler.handle/ClickHandler.handle value
line Click > Handler()/Handler.log value
known #100 line Click > Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log value
line Handler()/Handler.handle/ClickHandler.handle > Handler()/Handler.handle back
line Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log > Handler()/Handler.log back

home Handler Handler()
home Event Handler()
home Click Handler()

side entry left

# each override takes a value of its own class, and of the type its own signature names, from beyond; the Handler ends
# at the border of the dispatch
known #100 extra line Handler > Handler()/Handler.handle value
known #100 extra line Handler > Handler()/Handler.log value
known #100 extra line ClickHandler > Handler()/Handler.handle/ClickHandler.handle value
known #100 extra line ClickHandler > Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log value
known #100 extra line Named > Handler()/Handler.log/ClickHandler.log value
known #100 extra home ClickHandler Handler()
known #100 extra home Named Handler()
